The space bar, with or without Shift, fires keypress in Ladybird, with
the key " ", a keyCode and a charCode of 32, between keydown and
beforeinput, and canceling that keypress keeps the space out of a
textarea. Run headless with real key presses, Chrome 158.0.8127.38,
Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 all do the same. In their sources, Blink
dispatches keypress for the char event the platform makes for any key
that types text, in its KeyboardEventManager::KeyEvent(), and WebKit
for the char event its EventHandler::keyEvent() disambiguates. Gecko
dispatches it for every key but modifier and dead keys, as its
WidgetKeyboardEvent::ShouldCauseKeypressEvents() decides.
